    "comment": "Lead glaze on Clayworks greenware. Without this the whole mechanic is invisible to anyone working in Clayworks colours, because the greenware they hold is clayworks:-domain. Which path each file needs was read from the files themselves: most declare class: \"Block\" or nothing (so `add /class` is right), but the flowerpot and planter declare classByType: {\"*\": \"Block\"}, whose catch-all would overwrite a plain /class at solveByType time \u2014 those get the ByType entry replaced instead.",
